  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the arithmetic mean of outcomes without regard to probabilities, which involves comparing 1250 (A) and 1200 (B). However, the individual explicitly disregards the outcome difference and instead focuses on probabilities, ultimately choosing based on a slightly higher probability of winning. The information considered by the individual (probabilities and relative outcome indifference) does not align with the information required by the decision reason (raw mean of outcomes). Furthermore, the justification—choosing based on higher probability after deeming outcomes similar—is fundamentally different from the rule of the decision reason, which would favor A due to higher average outcome. There is no indication that the individual computed or considered the mean of outcomes in the way specified. Therefore, it is unlikely that the decision reason was used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
